HNG Ride-Sharing SQL Business Analysis (Stage 2)

Project Overview
This project involved a deep-dive business health audit of HNG Ride, a ride-sharing platform. 
Using SQL, I analyzed large-scale relational databases containing information on riders, drivers, rides, and payments. 
The goal was to evaluate operational efficiency, revenue growth, and rider retention between June 2021 and December 2024.

Objectives
Evaluate driver performance and identify top-tier earners for bonus eligibility.
Analyze quarterly and yearly revenue trends to identify growth patterns.
Measure rider retention and loyalty over a four-year period.
Identify high-value routes by analyzing the longest completed trips.

Technical Workflow (SQL Queries)
Operational Performance:
Joined rides, drivers, and riders tables to extract data on trip distances and pickup/drop-off locations.
Filtered datasets to include only "Completed" rides with "Successful" payments to ensure data accuracy.

Financial Analysis:
Calculated Year-over-Year (YoY) and Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ) revenue growth using aggregate functions.
Identified the top 10 longest completed rides by distance.

Driver Metrics & Bonus Logic:
Created complex queries to filter drivers based on three criteria:
  -Minimum of 30 completed rides.
  -Static rating of 4.5 or higher.
  -Cancellation rate lower than 5%.

Customer Retention:
Analyzed rider behavior to determine the percentage of repeat customers vs. one-time users.

Key Insights
Revenue Growth: The platform showed consistent revenue expansion, with specific quarters showing sharp peaks due to increased rider engagement.

Driver Efficiency: Out of the entire fleet, only a select few (e.g., Driver 1005 and 1181) met the high-performance criteria for the management bonus, highlighting a need for driver optimization.

Service Standards: Maintained strong rider loyalty through high service standards, as evidenced by consistent ratings among the top-performing drivers.

Tools Used
SQL: For data extraction, joining tables, and complex business logic.
Database Environment: PostgreSQL.
